 "response": "Vekre's budget is now **$1625K**.\n\n**Method**\n- Only Finance Office messages change the budget. All other messages (Marketing, Engineering, Operations, PMO, Sales, Legal, Vendor, Facilities) were ignored.\n- Finance Office entries that don't touch the budget (purchase orders, audits, room changes and similar) were ignored.\n- The starting point is #0001, which sets the budget to $2550K.\n- Each withdrawal chain was followed to its end. A withdrawal counts only if it is not itself withdrawn by a later effective withdrawal. For example:\n  - #1250 withdraws #0177, which withdrew #0091, which withdrew #0012, which withdrew #0010. Since #1250 stands, #0091 applies, #0012 is undone, and #0010 (\u2212$134K) applies.\n  - #1126 withdraws #0586, which withdrew #0431, which withdrew #0150. Since #1126 stands, #0431 applies, #0150 is undone, and #0130 (\u2212$131K) applies.\n  - #1556 withdraws #1165, which withdrew #0908. Since #1556 stands, #0908 applies and #0412 (+$151K) is removed.\n- About 125 Finance Office updates end up withdrawn, including #0004, #0008, #0015, #0024, #0036, #0890, #1045 and #1392.\n\n**Result**\n- All remaining Finance Office increases and decreases were applied once each, in record order, after the $2550K starting value.\n- This was a single pass; I did not do a separate check of the running total.\n\nANSWER: $1625K",
